+# Add t and use it to validate PlaceBlock arguments
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker as a dependency, so we can validate remote arguments with it now and in remotes we add later.
+- Switches the `PlaceBlock` handler in `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau` from hand-written `typeof` checks to a `t` checker.
+
+## Changes
+
+### `pesde.toml`
+
+This repo installs packages with pesde, which pulls Wally packages through `[wally_indices]`. There's no `wally.toml`. t goes into `[dependencies]`, pinned exactly like the other packages:
+
+```toml
+t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }
+```
+
+3.1.1 is the newest version on the Wally index. After installing, it's at `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`.
+
+### `BlockPlacement.server.luau`
+
+The argument checks are now one checker built once, when the module loads:
+
+```lua
+local finiteVector3 = t.intersection(t.Vector3, function(value: Vector3) ... end)
+local checkPlaceBlockArgs = t.tuple(t.string, finiteVector3)
+```
+
+It does the same checks as before:
+
+| Check before | Check now |
+| --- | --- |
+| `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.string` |
+| `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` |
+| `position ~= position` (rejects NaN) | the custom predicate in `finiteVector3`. **`t.Vector3` doesn't reject NaN by itself**, so this predicate is needed. |
+
+All the checks after that are unchanged: the block type must exist in `BlockTypes.ByName`, the per-player rate limit, the character/`HumanoidRootPart` check, `cell.Y < 0`, the occupied cell, and `MAX_REACH`. Like before, extra arguments beyond the first two are ignored. Invalid requests are still dropped without an error or a warning.
+
+## Before testing (reviewer steps)
+
+1. **Install packages.** The `t` package isn't in `roblox_packages/` yet, and until it is, `BlockPlacement` errors at `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)`. Run this from the repo root:
+   ```sh
+   pesde install
+   ```
+   (pesde is pinned in `rokit.toml`. Run `rokit install` first if you don't have it.)
+2. **Commit the updated `pesde.lock`.** This PR changes `pesde.toml` but **doesn't** change `pesde.lock`, because it was written without running the install. The `pesde install` in step 1 updates the lockfile. Commit that change to this branch so everyone resolves the same t version.
+3. **Rebuild the sourcemap if you use luau-lsp** so it picks up the new `Packages.t` alias. Run `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json` or restart your editor's Rojo/luau-lsp integration.
+4. Run `rojo serve` (or rebuild the place) as usual.
+
+## Testing
+
+None of this has been run yet: no install, no build, no play test. Please check:
+
+- [ ] A normal block placement from the client still works.
+- [ ] From the server-side command bar or a test client, firing `PlaceBlock` with bad arguments places nothing and logs no errors:
+  - a non-string block type (e.g. `123`, `nil`)
+  - a non-Vector3 position (e.g. `"0,0,0"`, `CFrame.new()`, `nil`)
+  - a NaN position: `Vector3.new(0/0, 0, 0)`
+  - an unknown block type name (e.g. `"Bedrock"`)
+- [ ] The rate limit, reach limit, below-ground, and occupied-cell rejections still work.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
